From: Armada / upstream 7.3, adapted for Asgard
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: LPASS releases its ADSP votes in sleep, so CX can collapse

Replaces 9040. Ported from Armada PR #723 (Odin 3, SM8750: CXSD + DDR LPM in
s2idle, 7.8 mA over 4 h):
- 0557-0562: upstream 7.3 (Ajay Kumar Nandam) wsa/va/tx/rx macros under the PM
  clock framework, so the q6prm LPASS_HW_MACRO/DCODEC votes the 7.2 drivers hold
  from probe drop in runtime suspend. On the Thor all four macros sat
  runtime-suspended with LPASS_HW_MACRO/DCODEC still at enable count 4.
- 0563/0564/0565 (sm8650 -> sm8550 LPI): macros, SoundWire and the LPASS LPI pin
  controller force-runtime-suspend across system sleep.
- 0531, rewritten for our sc8280xp.c (PRIMARY_MI2S_RX only): the board i2s_clk
  (the speaker MI2S) is dropped in suspend_post and retaken in resume_pre, so a
  PCM open at suspend doesn't keep it.
These votes are the ADSP's "AUDIO" DRV in the AOP CXPC violator list; with them
held, AOP never does CX shutdown (cxsd/aosd counts 0).

diff -ruN a/sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig b/sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig
diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8550-lpass-lpi.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8550-lpass-lpi.c
index 875e04e5d2b9..4c565b9d6486 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8550-lpass-lpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8550-lpass-lpi.c
@@ -213,6 +213,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id lpi_pinctrl_of_match[] = {
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, lpi_pinctrl_of_match);
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops lpi_pinctrl_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(pm_clk_suspend, pm_clk_resume, NULL)
 };
 
diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 55678a30cd4a..832bf25282c1 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1826,6 +1826,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops swrm_dev_pm_ops = {
+	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(swrm_runtime_suspend, swrm_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
index 282a6aaa9986..8e83824424f0 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
@@ -3997,6 +3997,7 @@ static int rx_macro_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops rx_macro_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(rx_macro_runtime_suspend, rx_macro_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
index a8e83eb60ba2..d40ac1c403d1 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
@@ -2435,6 +2435,7 @@ static int tx_macro_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops tx_macro_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(tx_macro_runtime_suspend, tx_macro_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
index dbc5795b9273..0ed9f9472b70 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
@@ -1765,6 +1765,7 @@ static int va_macro_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops va_macro_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(va_macro_runtime_suspend, va_macro_runtime_resume, NULL)
